    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/spec/definitions/@D002/definition",
      "value": "For a subset A of a metric or extended metric space X, diam(A)=sup{d(x,y):x,y∈A} in [0,∞], where d is its (extended) distance and sup∅=0. Thus diam∅=0. When diam(A)≤a<∞ we treat it as the corresponding finite nonnegative real number. Countable sums of nonnegative quantities mean the supremum of finite partial sums, and may be infinite; powers with positive exponent have 0^s=0 and ∞^s=∞."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
